# ============================================================================
#  Max Agency - MODEL CONFIGURATION  (edit the values; one model id per role)
# ============================================================================
#
# This is the single place to set which model each role uses. The gate reads it
# on every run. After editing, test with:   python gate/check_model.py <role>
#
# Precedence (highest first):
#   1. a CLI flag                       (--coder-model ...)
#   2. the PROJECT's own Max_AgencyConfig.md file (in that repo's root) <-- preferred
#      per-project mechanism; setup.ps1 creates it. The gate reads it each run.
#   3. a shell environment variable     (GATE_CODER_MODEL=...)
#   4. this file
#   5. a built-in fallback
# So this file is the GLOBAL default across all repos; to give ONE project a
# different model (e.g. a writing model for a book repo), edit that repo's
# Max_AgencyConfig.md instead of this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  CODER  - writes the actual code/content. Runs through hermes (in WSL), which
#  routes to OpenRouter. The value is an OpenRouter model id of the form
#  "provider/model" - the provider is part of the id, and ONE OpenRouter key
#  (below) covers them all. Browse ids at https://openrouter.ai/models
#    * code projects -> a strong coding model, e.g.  xiaomi/mimo-v2.5
#    * prose/story/book projects -> a strong writing model, e.g.
#        anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6   or   openai/gpt-5.4   (pick per taste/cost)
GATE_CODER_MODEL=xiaomi/mimo-v2.5
#
#  ORCHESTRATOR  - triage + kickoff expansion. Runs through the `codex` CLI
#  (OpenAI / your ChatGPT-account login). Must be a model that login accepts.
GATE_TRIAGE_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini
#
#  ARCHITECT / CTO  - planning + PR review. Run through the `claude` CLI
#  (Anthropic login). Use a Claude alias ("opus"/"sonnet"/"haiku") or a full id.
GATE_ARCHITECT_MODEL=opus
GATE_CTO_MODEL=opus
#
# ============================================================================
#  API KEYS  (where each provider's credentials live - NOT in this file)
# ============================================================================
#  * CODER / OpenRouter : OPENROUTER_API_KEY in  ~/.hermes/.env  (WSL filesystem).
#      Set/verify:  wsl -e bash -lc "grep -c OPENROUTER_API_KEY ~/.hermes/.env"
#      One key works for every provider/model OpenRouter offers.
#  * ORCHESTRATOR / codex : `codex` CLI auth (ChatGPT account or OpenAI API key).
#      Sign in once:  codex   (then /login)   - verify: codex --version
#  * ARCHITECT+CTO / claude : `claude` CLI auth (Anthropic).
#      Sign in once:  claude  (then /login)
# ============================================================================
